CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
`sink = *d`, with `d` pointing to `dA` or `dB` and the matching mutex
held, is lowered to `d == &dA ? dA : dB`. Renaming both branches with the
plain path guard recorded a shared READ of both objects, so with
`d == &dB` main was seen reading `dA` while holding `mB`, and paired with
the thread's write of `dA` under `mA`. The program reads only what `d`
points to: each branch of an `if` is now renamed under its condition.

Reported FAILED before the fix, SUCCESSFUL after. Also fixes the
`ctl_local` reduction of the goblint 09-regions family.

See `pointer_read_target_race`: the same read with the locks swapped
really races, and must stay FAILED.
